 little  more  but i think this really shows the  importance of sequencing  because working on the assumption that  all the s gene dropouts  were the uk variant would have resulted  in misreporting for this variant  and that can complicate disease tracking  and all sorts of things  so looking at  the data we're able to see  that so what i'm showing here is two of  our other samples of the first two igb  tracks and then sample eight as the  third igb  track and you can clearly see that  deletion  69-70 on the left  is present in sample eight but  deletion y one four four is not observed  in  snap light and that was one of our first  indications  that this sample was not the k variant  this this variant again our sample 8  again  didn't have n 501 y which we know  is an important mutation um  there was enough depth at that  uh locus in sample eight for appropriate  germline variant calling  but it was all wild type we did not see  the n501y which we saw in the other  uk various samples  in addition um there were other  mutations observed in sampling that were  not  known uk variant uk variants and were  not seen in the other samples  so what was this sample a  ended up being b1 375  which is not a variant of concern right  so and i'm showing here a phylogeny map  from next clade  and you can see that red dot is  is sample eight right  um and it you know and i think this just  again brings home  that this could have been misreported  based on the pcr results alone  but that sequencing really made it clear  what this sample was and what it wasn't  so swift uh just to wrap up  swiss is really focused on empowering  um data right  by sequencing we also  in in addition to our snap sars  assay we also have rna kits  um if someone's looking to do rna-seq  we can we can  make libraries from as little as 10  nanograms of total rna  our swift excel and gs methyl seek  product can unlock epigenetic insights  so for methylation of a sample  and we can also do host research  um for with generating whole genome  libraries from as little as one nanogram  with our swift sonic 2s library prep  thank you for listening to this webinar  um  i hope you learned something and please  get in contact if you have  any questions or would like to learn  more  thank you
 

